   "id": "S6_ala",
   "rule": "alā followed by an imperfect verb (offer/urging/question: tuḥibbūna, tuqātilūna, yaẓunnu, taʾkulūna, tattaqūna...) → stress lām. alā as attention-getter (usually before inna / a nominal clause / lahu) → stress hamza. If the morphology source tags the word as INC (inceptive particle) → hamza; if it splits it into interrogative hamza + negative lā → lām. Exclude allā (an + lā, written with shadda). With wāw/fāʾ between hamza and lā (awalā, afalā) → lām.",
   "examplesLam": [
    "24:22",
    "9:13",
    "83:4",
    "51:27",
    "26:106"
   ],
   "examplesHamza": [
    "2:12",
    "10:62",
    "7:54"
   ]
  },
