  {
   "id": "P3_heavy_madd",
   "level": "strong",
   "rule": "Madd lāzim kalimī muthaqqal (long vowel + doubled letter): strong stress at the end of the long vowel, dropping onto the doubled letter. Colour the doubled letter. Exclude doubled mīm/nūn (ghunna replaces it) and, at a pause, final qalqala letters (dawābb, al-ḥājj).",
   "examples": [
    "1:7 الضَّالِّينَ",
    "2:164 دَابَّةٍ",
    "6:80 أَتُحَاجُّونِّي",
    "80:33 الصَّاخَّةُ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "P3_doubled_waw_ya",
   "level": "strong",
   "rule": "Stress the letter BEFORE a doubled wāw or yāʾ (quwwa, ʿaduww, al-ḥayy, al-ghayy, iyyāka, al-qayyūm, al-jūdiyy), joining and pausing."
